INSERT INTO seo_pages (path, intro) VALUES
  ('/browse/us/arizona/phoenix', $cityText$Phoenix is the capital of Arizona and the center of the Valley of the Sun, a metro area that also takes in Scottsdale, Tempe, Mesa, Chandler and Glendale. People here use local classifieds all year, but the seasons shape what they look for. When summer temperatures climb past 100°F, listings for air conditioning repair, pool service, window tinting and car detailing fill up fast, and used cooling equipment sells quickly.

Winter brings visitors who stay for the mild weather, so short-term rooms, furnished rentals and event help are popular between November and April. Spring training baseball draws crowds to the Cactus League stadiums every March, which means extra demand for part-time work, parking and ride-sharing.

Tempe is home to Arizona State University, so student housing, textbooks, bikes and furniture move through the listings every August and May. Commutes can be long across the Valley, so many ads mention the nearest freeway or light rail stop. Whether you are selling a truck, offering handyman work or looking for a roommate, tell people which part of the Valley you are in. On BackpageNew Phoenix you can browse every category for free, post your own ad with pictures, and meet people in public places in daylight when you can.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/nevada/las-vegas', $cityText$Las Vegas runs on hospitality and entertainment, and its classifieds show it. The Strip, Fremont Street downtown and the resorts of Summerlin and Henderson employ people around the clock, so shift work, bartending, dealing, housekeeping, valet and event staffing are some of the most searched jobs. Many workers keep irregular hours, which is why ads often say exactly which days and times a person is free.

The city also hosts huge conventions and sporting events at the Convention Center, T-Mobile Arena and Allegiant Stadium. Around those dates, short rentals, rooms, car services and ticket swaps get busy, so it pays to be careful and to avoid anyone who asks for payment before you have seen something in person.

Because many residents moved here from other states, listings for furniture, moving help and storage are always in demand, and the desert climate means shade covers, evaporative coolers and pool equipment sell all year. Neighborhoods such as Henderson, North Las Vegas and the Southwest valley are often named in ads so buyers know how far they must drive. Browse Las Vegas classifieds and personals on BackpageNew by category, and when you post, add clear pictures, an honest description and the part of the valley you serve.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/colorado/denver', $cityText$Denver sits at about 5,280 feet above sea level, which is where its nickname, the Mile High City, comes from. Mountains are an hour or two to the west, and that shapes the local classifieds more than almost anything else. Skis, snowboards, bikes, climbing gear, camping equipment and roof racks are listed all year, with the biggest swings in autumn and spring when people trade gear for the next season.

The metro stretches from Boulder and Westminster in the north to Aurora, Centennial and Highlands Ranch in the south. Neighborhoods like LoDo, Capitol Hill, Highland and Cherry Creek come up often in rental and roommate listings, and landlords here regularly state whether a place allows pets or includes parking, which can be hard to find downtown.

Denver has a strong tech, healthcare and construction job market, plus a large craft brewing scene that creates hospitality openings. Vehicle listings frequently mention four-wheel drive and snow tires, a good clue about how people actually use their cars here. If you are new to the area, use the BackpageNew Denver categories to find services, jobs and housing close to where you live, and meet in a public place when you buy or sell.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/north-carolina/charlotte', $cityText$Charlotte is North Carolina's largest city and one of the biggest banking centers in the country, with the tall towers of Uptown holding offices for major financial companies. That steady flow of professionals moving in and out means rentals, roommate searches, furniture and moving services are among the busiest listings.

Neighborhoods have their own character. South End and NoDa attract people who want restaurants, breweries and art close by, Plaza Midwood and Dilworth are known for older homes and tree-lined streets, and the suburbs of Matthews, Huntersville and Ballantyne appeal to families. Ads that name the neighborhood or the nearest LYNX light rail stop get better answers because buyers know how far they must travel.

The Carolinas also have deep racing roots, and the NASCAR Hall of Fame is downtown, so automotive parts, trailers and repair services show up often. When the Carolina Panthers or Charlotte FC play at home, tickets and parking spaces change hands quickly, so be cautious with anything that sounds too good. Charlotte's mild spring and fall also bring a wave of outdoor and landscaping work. Use BackpageNew Charlotte to browse local classifieds and personal ads by category, and post your own with pictures and an honest description.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/louisiana/new-orleans', $cityText$New Orleans is known for the French Quarter, jazz, Mardi Gras and some of the best food in the country, and local classifieds follow the festival calendar. Around Carnival season, Jazz Fest and big events at the Superdome, people list costumes, tickets, spare rooms, parking spaces and short-term help. Musicians post ads looking for bandmates, lessons and gigs, especially in neighborhoods like the Marigny, Bywater and Treme.

Restaurants and hotels employ a large share of the city, so cooks, servers, bartenders, tour guides and drivers are in steady demand. Many of these ads mention evening hours and weekends, and some are seasonal, so it helps to say when you are available.

Housing here is a mix of shotgun houses, apartments and doubles in neighborhoods such as the Garden District, Uptown, Mid-City and Algiers, and landlords often explain flood risk, parking and utilities. Because parts of the city lie below sea level and hurricane season runs from June through November, you will also see listings for generators, storm shutters, tarps and repair work. If you are visiting or moving to New Orleans, browse BackpageNew by category, and always meet new people in a public place and tell a friend where you are going.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/texas/san-antonio', $cityText$San Antonio is one of the largest cities in Texas, famous for the Alamo, the River Walk and a strong local culture shaped by its Mexican American heritage. Visitors fill the downtown hotels all year, so hospitality, tour, driving and event jobs are a large part of the local listings.

The city is also a major military town, with Joint Base San Antonio and several training facilities nearby. Service members and their families regularly look for housing near the bases, trade vehicles and furniture when they move, and offer childcare or lawn care in nearby neighborhoods. Listings that mention the base or the closest highway get answered faster.

Spurs games, the Fiesta celebration each April and events at the Pearl and Southtown draw crowds, creating demand for tickets, catering help and rides. North of the city, the Texas Hill Country brings listings for horses, trailers, boats and ranch work. Summers are long and hot, so air conditioning, pool and auto repair services are in demand. Use BackpageNew San Antonio to browse categories for free, post your own ad with clear pictures and a fair price, and meet buyers or sellers in public, well-lit places.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/minnesota/minneapolis', $cityText$Minneapolis and neighboring St. Paul form the Twin Cities, a metro area with lakes inside the city limits, a long winter and a lively summer. That contrast shows up in the classifieds. From November to March, snow blowers, winter tires, shoveling and plowing services, and furnace repair are everywhere. Once the ice melts, listings turn to kayaks, paddleboards, bikes, patio furniture and lawn work.

The University of Minnesota keeps student housing, sublets, books and used furniture moving, especially around late August and May. Neighborhoods such as Uptown, Northeast, Dinkytown and Longfellow appear often in rental and roommate ads, and many mention skyway access or bus and light rail routes because people commute in cold weather.

Several large companies are based in the area and the Mall of America in nearby Bloomington is a major employer, so retail, healthcare and office roles show up all year. Fans buy and sell tickets for the Vikings, Twins, Timberwolves and Wild, so be careful and avoid sending money to someone you have not met. On BackpageNew Minneapolis you can browse classifieds and personal ads by category, and post your own with an honest description and the neighborhood you are in.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/pennsylvania/pittsburgh', $cityText$Pittsburgh is built around three rivers, the Allegheny, the Monongahela and the Ohio, and a landscape of steep hills and more than four hundred bridges. That geography matters in classifieds, because buyers and renters want to know which neighborhood an item or apartment is in and how steep the street is. Shadyside, Squirrel Hill, Lawrenceville, the Strip District and the South Side come up again and again.

The city has reinvented itself around education, healthcare, robotics and technology. Carnegie Mellon University and the University of Pittsburgh bring thousands of students every year, so furniture, bikes, textbooks and short-term rooms move quickly each August and May. Hospitals and research labs create steady demand for roommates and professional services.

Pittsburgh also loves its sports teams, the Steelers, the Pirates and the Penguins, and game days mean tickets, parking spaces and tailgating gear in the listings. Winters can be cold and snowy, which means snow removal, tire changes and home repair work are popular, while spring brings gardening and moving help. Use BackpageNew Pittsburgh to browse local categories, post your own ad with clear pictures, and meet in a public place whenever you buy, sell or meet someone new.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/arizona/tucson', $cityText$Tucson sits in the Sonoran Desert about two hours south of Phoenix, surrounded by mountains and tall saguaro cactus. It has a smaller, slower feel than the capital, and local classifieds reflect a mix of university life, military families, retirees and outdoor lovers.

The University of Arizona dominates the center of town, so student sublets, furniture, bikes and part-time jobs appear in large numbers every August and May. Davis-Monthan Air Force Base brings service members and families who look for housing, vehicles and childcare nearby. Many retirees and seasonal residents arrive for the warm winters, creating demand for furnished rentals, handyman work, yard care and caregiving.

Early each year the Tucson Gem and Mineral Show turns the city into a huge marketplace for stones, jewelry and crafts, and vendors and visitors list rooms, booths and transport. Summer monsoon storms bring roof repair, drainage work and car detailing, while triple-digit heat means cooling services are always needed. Hiking, cycling and camping gear sells steadily thanks to Saguaro National Park and Mount Lemmon. Browse Tucson classifieds and personal ads on BackpageNew, and when you post, mention your neighborhood so people know how far to drive.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/ohio/cleveland', $cityText$Cleveland sits on the shore of Lake Erie, and the lake shapes the weather, the work and the weekends. Lake-effect snow means snow blowers, plowing, roof repair and winter tires are popular listings, while summer brings boats, kayaks, patio furniture and landscaping help.

The city has a deep base in healthcare and education. The Cleveland Clinic and University Hospitals employ huge numbers of people around University Circle, which is also home to Case Western Reserve University and many museums. That creates constant demand for apartments, roommates, furniture and moving help in Cleveland Heights, Ohio City, Tremont, Lakewood and Shaker Heights.

Cleveland also has a strong manufacturing and trades background, so listings for tools, trucks, welding, carpentry and equipment repair are common. Fans buy and sell tickets for the Browns, the Guardians and the Cavaliers, and the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame and West Side Market bring visitors who sometimes need short rentals and tour help. Many older houses here need repair work, so contractors and handymen post often. Use BackpageNew Cleveland to browse categories by neighborhood, post your own ad with clear pictures and an honest price, and meet new people in a public place.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/nebraska/omaha', $cityText$Omaha is Nebraska's largest city, set on the Missouri River on the eastern edge of the state. It has a reputation for friendly neighborhoods, steady jobs and an affordable cost of living, and the local classifieds reflect a practical, community-minded city.

Insurance, finance, healthcare, logistics and food companies employ a large share of residents, and Offutt Air Force Base in nearby Bellevue brings military families who regularly search for housing, vehicles and childcare. Neighborhoods such as the Old Market, Dundee, Benson, Midtown and West Omaha come up often in rental, roommate and service ads.

Every June the city hosts the Men's College World Series, and in the weeks around it listings for tickets, spare rooms, parking and short-term work jump. Henry Doorly Zoo and the Old Market draw visitors all year. Winters are cold and summers can be hot and humid, so snow removal, furnace repair, lawn care and tree work are popular. Farm and ranch equipment, trailers and pickup trucks also sell well because the region is closely tied to agriculture. Browse Omaha classifieds and personal ads on BackpageNew by category, and when you post, add pictures, a fair price and the part of town you are in.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/indiana/indianapolis', $cityText$Indianapolis is the capital of Indiana and sits near the center of the state, with highways in every direction that earned it the title Crossroads of America. Shipping, logistics, manufacturing and healthcare are major employers, and the city is home to the headquarters of pharmaceutical and insurance companies, so steady work and relocations keep housing and furniture listings busy.

Motorsports are woven into local life. Each May the Indianapolis 500 at the Indianapolis Motor Speedway brings visitors from around the world, and in the weeks before it, listings for rooms, parking, tickets and event work appear daily. Throughout the year, Colts and Pacers games downtown bring more ticket and parking offers.

Neighborhoods such as Broad Ripple, Fountain Square, Mass Ave, Irvington and Carmel in the northern suburbs are often named in rental and roommate ads. The city's four distinct seasons mean lawn care, landscaping and snow removal are in demand almost year-round. Auto repair, trailer and truck listings are common given how much people drive. On BackpageNew Indianapolis you can browse every category for free, post your own ad with clear pictures and honest details, and arrange to meet in a public place, ideally during the day.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/new-york/buffalo', $cityText$Buffalo is the second-largest city in New York State, located at the eastern end of Lake Erie right beside the Canadian border. Its winters are famous for lake-effect snow, and that is the first thing you notice in the classifieds: snow blowers, plowing, shoveling, winter tires and roofing work are listed in huge numbers from November to March.

The city is known for Buffalo wings, which were first served at a local bar, and for loyal fans of the Bills and the Sabres. Tickets, parking and game-day services trade hands every season. Niagara Falls is only about twenty miles away, so tour guides, drivers and seasonal hotel or restaurant staff are often needed, and cross-border shoppers and workers use the Peace Bridge.

Neighborhoods such as Elmwood Village, Allentown, North Buffalo, Kenmore and the waterfront area around Canalside are often named in rental, roommate and service ads. Buffalo has many older homes, so carpentry, painting, plumbing and renovation help are common listings, and rents have traditionally been lower than in many large cities. Use BackpageNew Buffalo to browse classifieds and personal ads by category, post your own ad with pictures and a fair description, and meet new people in a public place.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/missouri/kansas-city', $cityText$Kansas City stretches across the Missouri and Kansas state line, and its identity is built on barbecue, jazz and fountains. Local classifieds include listings on both sides of the line, so it helps to say which side you are on, especially for rentals and services.

The Country Club Plaza, the Crossroads Arts District, Westport, the River Market and Brookside are popular neighborhoods, and midtown has many older homes that need repairs, painting and landscaping. Artists and musicians list studios, lessons and gigs, and the city's jazz history lives on in small clubs and festivals.

On game days, fans buy and sell tickets for the Chiefs at Arrowhead Stadium and the Royals at Kauffman Stadium, and tailgating gear, parking and event help appear in the listings. Barbecue restaurants and catering companies hire cooks, servers and drivers, and food trucks regularly look for helpers. Because Kansas City is a large distribution and rail hub, jobs in warehouses, trucking and logistics are common. The region also has hot summers and cold winters, so heating, cooling and yard work stay in demand. Browse Kansas City classifieds on BackpageNew by category, post your own ad with clear pictures, and meet in a public place.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/california/los-angeles', $cityText$Los Angeles is a huge, spread-out city of neighborhoods, from Downtown and Hollywood to Silver Lake, Echo Park, Venice and the San Fernando Valley. Because distances are long and traffic can be heavy, the best classified ads say exactly which neighborhood or freeway exit you are near.

The entertainment industry shapes much of the local market. Actors, extras, photographers, makeup artists, set builders, drivers and assistants post and search for gigs, lessons, studio space and equipment. Cameras, lighting, music gear and costumes change hands often, and many people do freelance and creative work on flexible schedules.

The weather is mild all year, so outdoor events, car culture and beach life are constant themes. You will find listings for used cars, motorcycles, bikes, surfboards and moving help. Housing is expensive and competitive, so rooms, sublets and roommate searches are among the most active ads, and it is wise to see a place in person before sending any money. Many residents come from abroad or other states and look for language lessons, tutors and local services. Use BackpageNew Los Angeles to browse classifieds and personal ads by category, post with clear pictures and an honest description, and meet new people in a public place and let a friend know where you are going.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/new-york/new-york', $cityText$New York City is made up of five boroughs, Manhattan, Brooklyn, Queens, the Bronx and Staten Island, and almost everything in its classifieds depends on which borough and which subway line you are on. Good ads name the neighborhood and the nearest stop, because most people travel on the subway, by bus or on foot.

Housing is the biggest topic. Apartments are small, rents are high and the market moves fast, so roommate searches, sublets, storage and moving help are always in demand. Be careful with anything that asks for a deposit or fee before you have seen the place and met the person in real life.

The city also has an unusual mix of industries. Finance, media, fashion, theater, restaurants, healthcare and education all hire, and many people work several part-time or freelance jobs. Musicians, dancers, photographers and models look for collaborators, and small businesses look for help with delivery, tutoring and events. Furniture, bikes and electronics get passed along constantly because moving in and out of apartments is so common. Browse New York classifieds and personal ads on BackpageNew by category, post your own ad with clear pictures and a fair description, and always arrange to meet in a busy public place.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/illinois/chicago', $cityText$Chicago sits on the shore of Lake Michigan and is organized around the Loop downtown and a grid of neighborhoods that each feel like a small town. Lincoln Park, Wicker Park, Logan Square, Lakeview, Hyde Park and Pilsen appear often in rental, roommate and service listings, and many ads mention the nearest L train stop because that is how most people get around.

The weather is a big theme. Winters are cold and windy, so snow removal, winter tires, heating repair and moving help are in demand from November to March. Summers bring street festivals, lakefront beaches and outdoor concerts, and tickets, bikes, patio furniture and event work trade hands.

Chicago has deep roots in trades, transportation, finance, healthcare and food, so listings for electricians, carpenters, drivers, cooks and warehouse workers are common. Universities including the University of Chicago, Northwestern and DePaul bring students every year, and furniture and sublets move quickly in late August and May. Sports fans buy and sell tickets for the Cubs, White Sox, Bulls, Bears and Blackhawks. Use BackpageNew Chicago to browse categories by neighborhood, post your own ad with clear pictures, and meet in a public place whenever you buy, sell or meet someone new.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/texas/houston', $cityText$Houston is the largest city in Texas and one of the most diverse in the country, with a metro area that sprawls in every direction. It is a center for energy, shipping, aerospace and medicine, with the Texas Medical Center and NASA's Johnson Space Center among its best-known institutions. These industries bring skilled workers from around the world, so rentals, roommate searches, relocation help and furniture are always among the busiest listings.

Because the city is so large, the best ads say which part of town they are in, such as Montrose, the Heights, Midtown, Katy, Sugar Land or The Woodlands. People rely on cars, so vehicle, truck and trailer listings are common and mention the highway you are near.

The climate is hot and humid, with a hurricane and storm season from June to November. That drives demand for air conditioning repair, generators, roof and flood damage repair, and car washing. Sports fans trade tickets for the Astros, Rockets and Texans, and the Houston Livestock Show and Rodeo draws large crowds each spring. Houston's food scene also creates cooking and catering work. Browse Houston classifieds and personal ads on BackpageNew by category, post with clear pictures and an honest price, and meet in a public place.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/georgia/atlanta', $cityText$Atlanta is the capital of Georgia and a major hub for business, film and travel. Hartsfield-Jackson is one of the busiest airports in the world, so airline, logistics and hospitality jobs are common, and Georgia's growing film and television industry creates openings for extras, crew, drivers, caterers and equipment rental.

The city is a patchwork of neighborhoods, including Midtown, Buckhead, Old Fourth Ward, Inman Park, East Atlanta and nearby Decatur. Because traffic on I-75, I-85 and the Downtown Connector can be heavy, people often list how far they are from the MARTA train and which highway exit is closest. That detail helps buyers, renters and customers decide quickly.

Atlanta is also a university city, home to Georgia Tech, Emory, Georgia State and the Atlanta University Center, and each fall and spring student housing, textbooks, bikes and furniture are listed in large numbers. Music, art and nightlife scenes mean that DJs, bands, photographers and promoters often look for collaborators. Fans trade tickets for the Braves, Falcons, Hawks and Atlanta United, and summer storms and heat bring work for roofers, landscapers and air conditioning technicians. Use BackpageNew Atlanta to browse every category for free, post your own ad with clear pictures, and meet in a public place.$cityText$),
  ('/browse/us/florida/miami', $cityText$Miami is warm all year, bilingual and international, and its classifieds feel that way. Many ads are written in English and Spanish, and neighborhoods such as Brickell, Wynwood, Little Havana, Coconut Grove, Doral and Kendall are named in rental, roommate and service listings. Miami Beach is a separate city next door, so it helps to say exactly where you are.

Tourism, hospitality, shipping, real estate and healthcare are among the biggest employers. Hotels, restaurants and clubs hire servers, bartenders, hosts, drivers and event staff, and many jobs are seasonal, peaking from late fall through spring. People also list boats, jet skis, fishing gear, scuba equipment and dock space because so much of life revolves around Biscayne Bay and the Atlantic.

Housing is expensive and the market moves quickly, so sublets, rooms and short-term rentals are some of the most active listings. Never send money before you have seen a place and met the person in real life. Hurricane season runs from June through November, which means generators, shutters and storm cleanup show up in the listings, and the heat keeps air conditioning and car detailing in demand. Fans trade tickets for the Heat, Dolphins and Marlins. Browse Miami classifieds and personal ads on BackpageNew by category, and meet in public places.$cityText$)
